# Project artefacts
# The JSON reports ARE tracked: the README cites specific numbers, and a measurement that is not
# versioned cannot be audited and can be quietly overwritten by the next run. That is exactly what
# happened to the old-taxonomy dataset report. `results/runs/` stays ignored - it is per-run
# visualiser output, large and reproducible.
results/*
!results/*.json
!results/*.md
# Bookings created by a live call. Personal data (a name and a phone number), and reproducible.
data/bookings.jsonl
.cache/

# OS
.DS_Store

# generated Kaggle upload folder (regenerate with training/make_kaggle_dataset.py)
kaggle/

# fine-tuned checkpoints (large; regenerated by training/kaggle_run.py)
models/

# downloaded third-party evaluation data (Banking77, CLINC150)
data/external/
